--TEST--
`Core\Uuid::format` writes the sixteen bytes `fromBytes` was given as hex in their order, with dashes after the 4th, 6th, 8th and 10th byte, and it is the same text when it is called as the `format` method `Parses` requires — `rule:routing/link-target-and-params-are-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Uuid::format
class Writer
{
    public static function written(Parses $value): tainted string
    {
        return $value->format();
    }
}

var $id = Core\Uuid::fromBytes(Core\Encoding::fromHex("00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff"));
echo $id->format(), "\n";
echo Writer::written($id), "\n";
echo Writer::written($id) == $id->format() ? "same" : "DIFFERENT", "\n";
--EXPECT--
00112233-4455-6677-8899-aabbccddeeff
00112233-4455-6677-8899-aabbccddeeff
same
